% ============================================================================
% planets.query.adj — a worked recall over the astronomy planets library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "which planet is third from
% the Sun?" — it states no astronomy fact, only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the `planet_order`
% rows and returns the position (or the planet, on a reverse query) + the NASA
% source/locator/trust. A body that is not one of the eight major planets abstains
% honestly — the engine never invents an order.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli planets.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "planets.adj"

? planet_order(earth, $N)          % expect 3  (which position is Earth?)
? planet_order(neptune, $N)        % expect 8  (the farthest major planet)
? planet_order($Planet, 1)         % expect mercury (reverse: who is nearest?)
? planet_order(pluto, $N)          % expect abstain — a dwarf planet, not a row
